.TH TRUNCATE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
truncate \- change the length of a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int truncate(const char* path, off_t length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets the file named by path to length bytes.  Extending a file reads back as
zero-filled bytes.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ftruncate (3crunch),
.BR truncate (2)
